    {
      "id": "MIG-07-FOUR-TIER-AUDIT",
      "title": "Four-tier compliance audit and real telemetry-candidate parity for the F# shadow CLI",
      "description": "Audit all Ros.Domain/Application/Contracts/Infrastructure/Cli source against SDE-DOCTRINE-003 (Four-Tier Architecture) for tier violations beyond the existing project-reference architecture test; none found. Close a real shadow/production parity gap: ros-fs work plan --resolve-telemetry only accepted synthetic --candidate flags, unlike every sibling observation (evidence, Git status) which reads real repository state by default. Add Ros.Infrastructure.Work.FileTelemetryStateRepository reading real .ros/telemetry/executions/*.json records and wire it as the CLI default; rewrite differential tests to read real fixture state instead of synthetic candidates. Document (but do not close in this slice) a second, larger gap: work context-plan's Git-observed-path composition, which needs a config-driven glob matcher and ROS_BASE_REF support that do not exist yet in F#.",
      "tags": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "status": "ready",
      "attachments": [],
